nifest, or the whole environment is dumped into it.\",\n   \"met\": \"yes\",\n   \"evidence\": \"src/agent/identity.ts:8\",\n   \"quote\": \"const CONFIG_FILES = [\\\"config/policy.yaml\\\", \\\"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\\\", \\\"config/budgets.yaml\\\"];\",\n   \"counter_search\": \"Listed every hashed input: digest, versions, prompt files, model ids and three config files; none holds secrets, and no environment is dumped.\",\n   \"note\": \"No secret values are hashed.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"red_flags_found\": [],\n \"violates\": [\n  \"hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration\"\n ],\n \"also_affects\": [\n  \"C03\"\n ],\n \"summary\": \"The type id skips prompts/system.md because it only hashes .txt files, so the system prompt can change without changing the id.\",\n \"next_step\": \"Hash every file under prompts/ (and the MCP server list), then add a test that changing each input changes the id.\",\n \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n}\n{\n \"item\": \"B04\",\n \"gate\": \"G1\",\n \"title\": \"Independent revocation\",\n \"requirement\": \"Show that an operator can cut off this agent's access without cutting off the user who launched it. The agent must not need to cooperate. Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect. Count cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions. A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit that fits the potential harm. Revoking only the refresh token is not enough. If tokens live longer than that limit, push the revocation to each service (for example, with OpenID CAEP session-revoked events) or make the tokens shorter-lived.\",\n \"not_covered\": [\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"A kill switch that doesn't stop running work or open tool streams\",\n   \"owner\": \"R11\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"Sub-agents or remote workers still acting after the parent is stopped\",\n   \"owner\": \"E09\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"problem\": \"Static API keys used 