e is a tag like `:latest`, a branch, a model alias, or a default that falls back to one.\",\n   \"met\": \"yes\",\n   \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:76\",\n   \"quote\": \"clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\",\n   \"counter_search\": \"Followed models (dated constants, config.ts:49-50) and prompts (copied into the image, Dockerfile:17); no tag or alias fallback.\",\n   \"note\": \"Image, prompts and models are fixed by digest or dated id.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"C03.2\",\n   \"check\": \"A process outside the agent observes the running artifacts (image digest, prompt, model, tool setup) and compares them with the approved manifest, rather than trusting what the agent reports.\",\n   \"verify\": \"1) Find a process outside the agent (admission controller, CI check, sidecar, scheduled job) that reads running artifacts. 2) Check it observes image digest, prompt, model, and tool setup itself and compares each with the approved manifest. 3) Answer no if it trusts values the agent reports, or compares a value with itself. Answer unknown if it would run in a platform outside this repo.\",\n   \"met\": \"unknown\",\n   \"evidence\": \"src/server.ts:32\",\n   \"quote\": \"if (typeId !== manifest.agentTypeId) {\",\n   \"counter_search\": \"\",\n   \"note\": \"The only comparison runs inside the agent process at startup. CI checks prompt files against the manifest, not the running pods, and deploy.yml only greps the digest. A platform observer is not shown.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"C03.3\",\n   \"check\": \"The emitted agent-type-id is computed from the observed running artifacts, so a changed prompt, model, weights file, or tool setup produces a different ID instead of the approved one.\",\n   \"verify\": \"1) Find where the emitted `agent.type.id` comes from. 2) Check it is computed from the observed running artifacts at start or deploy. 3) Answer no if it is a constant, an env var or config value set at build, or c