{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014VNWY2jbRmWxwNDHxAfoEt","type":"tool_result","content":"===== A03 Content-derived type identity gap high\nREQ: Compute the agent-type-id as a hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration. The model part includes checkpoint and fine-tune or adapter references where they apply. Keep the list of inputs (the manifest) and the hashing steps. Check that changing any input changes the ID, and that the same manifest gives the same ID.\nNOTCOV: [{\"problem\": \"Changed running config still reporting the old approved ID\", \"owner\": \"C03\"}, {\"problem\": \"Hosted model changing behind a fixed name\", \"owner\": \"C05\"}, {\"problem\": \"Release manifest missing training job, dataset, or model provider records\", \"owner\": \"C01\"}, {\"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\", \"owner\": \"A02\"}]\nEVID: [{\"file\": \"src/agent/identity.ts\", \"line\": 24, \"note\": \"The type id hashes only prompts/*.txt, so prompts/system.md, the system prompt, is not part of it. Image digest, harness version and sha, models and three config files are included.\"}]\nKEYS: ['item', 'gate', 'title', 'rating', 'confidence', 'red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role']\nalso_affects [\"C03\"]\nsummary \"The type id skips prompts/system.md because it only hashes .txt files, so the system prompt can change without changing the id.\"\n CHK A03.1 no src/agent/identity.ts:24 | .filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))\n CHK A03.2 no src/agent/identity.ts:24 | .filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))\n CHK A03.3 yes src/config.ts:49 | export const AGENT_MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\";\n CHK A03.4 yes src/agent/identity.ts:25 | .sort();\n CHK A03.5 yes src/agent/identity.ts:8 | const CONFIG_FILES = [\"config/policy.yaml\", \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\", \"config/budgets.yaml\"];\n===== B04 Independent revocation gap medium\nREQ: Show that an operator can cut off this agent's access without cutting off the user who launched it. The agent must not need to cooperate. Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect. Count cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions. A trusted enforcement point must block later calls within a time limit that fits the potential harm. Revoking only the refresh token is not enough. If tokens live longer than that limit, push the revocation to each service (for example, with OpenID CAEP session-revoked events) or make the tokens shorter-lived.\nNOTCOV: [{\"problem\": \"A kill switch that doesn't stop running work or open tool streams\", \"owner\": \"R11\"}, {\"problem\": \"Sub-agents or remote workers still acting after the parent is stopped\", \"owner\": \"E09\"}, {\"problem\": \"Static API keys used where short-lived credentials are available\", \"owner\": \"B03\"}, {\"problem\": \"No way to trace a suspicious action to its team, operator, and live instance\", \"owner\": \"A05\"}]\nEVID: []\nKEYS: ['item', 'gate', 'title', 'rating', 'confidence', 'red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role', 'challenge']\nalso_affects []\nsummary \"The agent has its own identity, but the revoke path, its time limit and its coverage of cached tokens are not in this repo.\"\n CHK B04.1 unknown infra/terraform/iam.tf:3 | resource \"aws_iam_role\" \"runtime\" {\n CHK B04.2 unknown  | \n CHK B04.3 no src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:34, src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:53 | if (hit && hit.exp - 30_000 > Date.now()) return hit.value;\nif (existing) return existing;\n CHK B04.4 unknown  | \n===== B05 Destructive-action interception gap high\nREQ: List the high-impact operations. These include deletes, destructive database updates, force-pushes, tearing down infrastructure, payment changes, and sending anything outside. Block them by default in the execution path. Allow one only when a reviewer or system with higher authority approves that specific action. When the action runs, authorize its operation, target, and arguments, and block it if they aren't allowed. A list of blocked words or command names is not enough. Test other tools and raw API or shell paths that could do the same thing. Treat deleting audit records, or changing how long they are kept, as high-impact too. That includes asking a more powerful tool or peer to do it. Some agents can do all three of these in one context: read untrusted input, reach sensitive data or systems, and change things or talk to the outside. For those agents, treat every consequential action as high-impact. The exception is a design that stops untrusted content from picking the tool, destination, or arguments. Examples are plan-then-execute, a two-model pattern, or capability tracking such as CaMeL. Record which of the three each agent type has.\nNOTCOV: [{\"problem\": \"Denied actions not recorded in the audit trail\", \"owner\": \"R13\"}, {\"problem\": \"Approvals that can be replayed, reused in parallel, or used after expiry\", \"owner\": \"B06\"}, {\"problem\": \"Outside effects left unreconciled after the agent is stopped\", \"owner\": \"R12\"}, {\"problem\": \"A chain of individually allowed actions that adds up to data theft\", \"owner\": \"R09\"}, {\"problem\": \"Tool output not labelled or kept apart from trusted instructions\", \"owner\": \"R02\"}]\nEVID: [{\"file\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\", \"line\": 17, \"note\": \"config/policy.yaml:5-8 lists cancel, refund and freeform SMS. But ehr__update_appointment can also set status to cancelled and is not listed, and the executor allows any tool not on the list (executor.ts:67). Deposit refunds are also made by insurance__check_eligibility, which is not listed.\"}]\nKEYS: ['item', 'gate', 'title', 'rating', 'confidence', 'red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role']\nalso_affects []\nsummary \"Cancel through ehr__update_appointment and th