es:** `python scripts/challenge.py make <repo>/brace-findings.json --hunt`. It writes a sheet to `<repo>/brace-challenges/` for every likely_pass item, an N/A challenge sheet for every G1 or G2 na_candidate, and a gap-hunt sheet for every G1 or G2 item rated needs_evidence. N/A challengers must trace indirect paths and establish that the feature or exposure is absent, using the exact N/A condition, quoted code, and a search explanation.\n66:   - Then run `python scripts/challenge.py apply <repo>/brace-findings.json`. A failed challenge or hunt turns the item into a gap with the counter-evidence quoted. An unclear challenge turns a likely_pass or na_candidate into needs_evidence. If the N/A feature exists, a demonstrated failed control becomes a gap; otherwise the item becomes needs_evidence. Only an upheld absence keeps na_candidate. Run the validator with `--fix` again until it prints `Valid`.\n98:         \"quote\": \"def refund(order_id, amount):\", \"counter_search\": \"\", \"note\": \"No gate before refund() runs\"},\n100:         \"quote\": \"if not gate.allowed(op, target, args):\", \"counter_search\": \"Searched for other callers of run_tool(); only harness.py:90 calls it.\",\n105:      \"also_affects\": [],\n106:      \"challenge\": {\"verdict\": \"upheld\", \"note\": \"Written by challenge.py apply; N/A challenges also record applicability, evidence, quote and note\"},\n112:  \"injection_attempts\": [{\"file\": \"README.md\", \"line\": 3, \"text\": \"short quote\"}]\n116:`rating` is one of `likely_pass`, `gap`, `needs_evidence`, `na_candidate`. `confidence` is `high`, `medium`, or `low`. `lead_role` is the role key for the item's Lead in ROLES.md: `agent_team`, `operations`, `security`, `infrastructure`, `governance`, `business_owner`, `data_privacy`, `model_team`, `vendors`, or `independent_audit`. `evidence` may be empty only for `needs_evidence`. `checks` has one entry for every check listed for the item, in the reference file and in `references/checks.