ildren, remote workers, queued work, and open tool streams, subscriptions, and tasks, where they exist. Check that the stop reaches every descendant within the set time. It must revoke access as needed and prevent orphaned retries or restarts. Record how outside effects that already happened are reconciled.\nNOTCOV: [{\"problem\": \"Agent able to disable or delay its own stop\", \"owner\": \"R11\"}, {\"problem\": \"No way to cut off the agent's access without cutting off the user\", \"owner\": \"B04\"}, {\"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type\", \"owner\": \"E12\"}, {\"problem\": \"Sub-agent given powers beyond its task\", \"owner\": \"E08\"}]\nEVID: [{\"file\": \"src/workers/reminders.ts\", \"line\": 33, \"note\": \"The reminder job checks the stop flag before each send and does not retry.\"}]\nKEYS: ['item', 'gate', 'title', 'rating', 'confidence', 'red_flags_found', 'violates', 'also_affects', 'summary', 'next_step', 'lead_role', 'challenge']\nalso_affects []\nsummary \"Stop aborts in-flight calls and the cron job checks the flag, but peer cancel, revocation and effect reconciliation are not shown.\"\n CHK E09.1 no src/control/kill-switch.ts:70 |           a.abort.abort(new Halted(halted.has(\"global\") ? \"global\" : `tenant#${a.tenantId}`));\n CHK E09.2 no src/control/kill-switch.ts:71, k8s/deployment.yaml:111 |           active.delete(runId);\n                  expirationSeconds: 900\n CHK E09.3 yes src/workers/reminders.ts:33 | await killSwitch.assertRunning(clinic.id);\n CHK E09.4 no src/control/kill-switch.ts:71 |           active.delete(runId);\n===== R12 Safe state after stopping gap medium\nREQ: Decide what happens to writes in progress, queued actions, and outside side effects. Where you can't cancel something, show how you check and fix the result (reconcile) or undo it another way (compensate). No restart may happen unattended, and no orphaned work may be left able to act.\nNOTCOV: [{\"problem\": \"Stop path depends on the