{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015HburTH2qpbMWGeH8DLDad","type":"tool_result","content":"A03 V: [\"hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration\"] RF: [] AA ['C03'] CH None\nB04 V: [\"Set and measure the longest time before the cutoff takes effect\", \"Count cached tokens, self-contained tokens, and open sessions\"] RF: [\"src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:34, src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:53 Cached EHR tokens (about 5 min) and MCP sessions (4 min, ehr-mcp.ts:66-69) are reused with no revocation check. IRSA sessions last up to 3600 s (iam.tf:5). No maximum revocation time is stated, and there is no CAEP, introspection or per-call check.\"] AA [] CH {'verdict': 'failed', 'note': \"Revoking the agent's own role is separable from users, but cached tokens and open sessions are reused with no per-call revocation check and no stated revocation limit.\"}\nB05 V: [\"Block them by default in the execution path\"] RF: [\"src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 A peer reply (depositWaived) triggers payments.refundDeposit with no approval, though payments__refund_deposit is a high-impact tool.\"] AA [] CH None\nB12 V: [\"Production deploys run only from CI on the reviewed branch\"] RF: [\".github/workflows/deploy.yml:6, .github/workflows/deploy.yml:51 Deploy is a manual workflow_dispatch. The emergency path deploys from any unreviewed hotfix/* branch, and the production-emergency environment allows branch_pattern hotfix/*. The checked-out branch supplies release/manifest.json and k8s/deployment.yaml, so a hotfix branch can deploy content that never went through the main branch's review. The commit is recorded, but the deploy is not limited to the reviewed branch.\"] AA [] CH {'verdict': 'failed', 'note': 'B12.3 fails because the workflow_dispatch emergency path deploys from unreviewed hotfix/* branches rather than only the reviewed branch.'}\nC03 V: [\"Test that a changed prompt, model, weights fil